# Animated Forms and Expand/Collapse

Whenever a button opens a form, or expands/collapses a section, the content must **animate** in and out—never appear or disappear statically.

## When this applies

- Buttons that reveal a form (e.g. "Add member", "Edit address", "Create household").
- Buttons or controls that expand/collapse a section (accordions, "Show more", toggles).
- Modals or panels that open/close in response to user action.

## Approach

- **In:** Use a short transition for opacity and/or height/transform (e.g. 150–300ms). Content should fade and/or slide in.
- **Out:** Use the same duration for exit so content fades and/or slides out before unmounting or hiding.
- **Implementation:** Prefer CSS transitions (`transition`, `transition-all`) with Tailwind (e.g. `transition-all duration-200 ease-out`). For enter/exit that requires unmounting, use a small delay before unmount so the exit animation can run, or use a library like `framer-motion` or React state that toggles a "closing" class.
- Keep animations subtle and fast enough not to feel sluggish (typically 200–300ms).

## Checklist when adding or changing UI

- [ ] Forms that open on button click animate in (and out when closed).
- [ ] Expand/collapse sections animate open and closed (height/opacity or similar).
- [ ] No instant show/hide for user-triggered content; always use a transition.
